# Test fixtures are DATA, not source. Their exact bytes — including line
# endings — are what the parser under test is asserted against, so git must
# never rewrite them.
#
# Why this exists: this repo is developed on Windows, where git's autocrlf
# converts LF to CRLF at checkout. `tools/segments/fixtures/*.vtt` were
# committed as LF and arrived as CRLF, which broke a test that constructs a
# CRLF variant from a fixture it assumed was LF (it produced "\r\r\n"). CI runs
# on Linux, so the failure was invisible there and only appeared on a developer
# checkout — the worst combination.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion for these paths in both
# directions. Scoped deliberately to fixtures rather than applied repo-wide:
# a blanket normalisation pass on a Windows checkout is its own well-known
# trap, and nothing here needs one.
tools/segments/fixtures/** -text
tools/transcribe/fixtures/** -text
backend/fixtures/** -text
